    "port (the variety work, round 2, Track S2: P4, topic threads): conversations of 3-6 turns between two bots (port/BotThreads), from 2004 player culture's topics: levels and the race to an unlock, what u doing, goals and saving up, members, how long u been playing, asl and where u from, drops, randoms, clans, the bank, school, Halo 2, World of Warcraft, Castle Wars next month, Zezima, the lag, food, music, films, being tired, a friend hacked, a million gp, Dragon Slayer, the weather.",
    "Each topic's pools by turn: 'ask' opens it (a's line), 'answer' the other's ({v}: its own value from its state: a level, what it does, where it lives ...), and the opener's own answer to a counter-question ('own'); 'lower'/'higher'/'same' the opener's own answer by how its value compares with the other's; 'after' the other's word on it ('afterLower' ... when it compares); 'more' a second question and its answers (depth 6 only: clique mates and hub regulars); 'follow' and 'followUp' when the pair talked of it earlier this session (bots only: 'still 41?', 'u get 50 yet?'), never asked again from scratch.",
    "Shared pools: 'counter' joins a counter-question to an answer ({x}: the answer): the asker then answers from its own state (the counter-question rule); 'segue' opens a second topic (once a thread); 'closers' end one now and then.",
    "Every line, its slots filled from every value they take, passes the 274 word filter and chat codec (test/chat-filter.test.mjs). The words are the period's: lower case, u/ur/r, no apostrophes, nothing after November 2004. Said in the speaker's style (port/BotStyle)."
